<title>UK: RESEARCH ALERT - Goldman downgrades Britannic.</title>
<headline>RESEARCH ALERT - Goldman downgrades Britannic.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-02-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>Goldman Sachs said on Wednesday it had cut its rating for Britannic Assurance Plc to &quot;market performer&quot; from &quot;trading buy&quot;.</p>
<p>Britannic announced a special bonus of 209 million stg for life insurance policies on Tuesday, following discussions with the government on ownership of surplus insurance funds.</p>
<p>Britannic shares were down three pence at 867 by 1231 GMT, after having jumped 63-1/2p on Tuesday.</p>
<p>-- London newsroom +44 171 542 4366</p>
